We can use the Euclidean algorithm to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of two numbers.
We divide the larger number, $29384$, by the smaller number, $10293$, and find the remainder.
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc}
&29384&\text{divided by }10293\\
\cline{2-3}
&\downarrow&\\
10293&2&\text{times}\\
&\downarrow&\\
&8798&\text{remainder}
\end{array}
\]
Next, we divide $10293$ by the remainder, $8798$, and find the new remainder.
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc}
&10293&\text{divided by }8798\\
\cline{2-3}
&\downarrow&\\
8798&1&\text{times}\\
&\downarrow&\\
&1495&\text{remainder}
\end{array}
\]
We continue this process until we reach a remainder of $0$.
\[
\begin{array}{c|cc}
&8798&\text{divided by }1495\\
\cline{2-3}
&\downarrow&\\
1495&5&\text{times}\\
&\downarrow&\\
&573&\text{remainder}
